[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794712678","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105250#issuecomment-2794712678","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105250","id":2794712678,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mk-5m","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T18:00:23Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T18:00:23Z","body":"@BastiaanOlij @mihe ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794712678/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2795374320","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105250#issuecomment-2795374320","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105250","id":2795374320,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mngbw","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T23:16:25Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T23:16:25Z","body":"Cool! I'm not familiar enough with the implementation to give a full thumbsup but will find some time to test this against my use case.\r\n\r\nAs already raised on RocketChat, we need to make sure:\r\n- This is supported with Jolt\r\n- This is correctly handled with GDExtension ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2795374320/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2796859327","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105250#issuecomment-2796859327","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105250","id":2796859327,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mtK-_","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T13:02:28Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T13:02:28Z","body":"I think this implementation is potentially quite CPU intensive: Let's say you have a scene with 10K objects and you put 1 object in the include list. That means you'll do a broadphase query on the 10K objects, possibly returning many intersecting objects and then loop over all those objects to check if the 1 object you're interested in is included.\r\n\r\nA better interface would be to be able to do a ray test on a single body RID. Then you can determine the 'include list' in your own application and simply iterate over the bodies to see if there's a hit. If the ray test starts by checking the bounding box of the body then it should easily beat using the technique above.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2796859327/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800383434","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105250#issuecomment-2800383434","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105250","id":2800383434,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m6nXK","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-14T03:30:21Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T03:30:21Z","body":"@jrouwe I didn't realise that is what the current approach would have as a drawback. When specifying a single or limited number of physics bodies in the include list, one would expect only those bodies to be evaluated, not just filtered from a larger broad phase result set.\r\n\r\nFor my use case being able to do a dedicated ray test on a single physics body RID would suffice so I would be happy with such a solution. That said, making it part of the already existing ray testing does make more sense from an API perspective. Could we do a best of both worlds approach where if we supply an include list, we skip the broad phase and instead test against the provided RIDs?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800383434/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2802830415","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105250#issuecomment-2802830415","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105250","id":2802830415,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nD8xP","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-14T19:49:28Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T19:49:28Z","body":"> one would expect only those bodies to be evaluated, not just filtered from a larger broad phase result set.\r\n\r\nThe implementation in the PR uses the broad phase result set as far as I can see (which is why I brought this up).\r\n\r\n> Could we do a best of both worlds approach where if we supply an include list, we skip the broad phase and instead test against the provided RIDs?\r\n\r\nYes, you could certainly do that. My objection to this would be that these kinds of 'swiss army knife' APIs usually end up being confusing. E.g. if you look at the current parameter set of `intersect_point`:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b93f1395-0753-47bc-a7f2-758ad08e0e0e)\r\n\r\nThen when you have an `include` list, 4 out of 5 parameters don't really make sense anymore:\r\n\r\n* `collide_with_areas`\r\n* `collide_with_bodies`\r\n* `collision_mask`\r\n* `exclude`\r\n\r\nFor each of these you'd need to specify if they still do something and how they co-operate with the `include` list. E.g. why would you first specify a body to `include` and then set `collide_with_bodies = false`. All that does is add overhead to the system because you'd probably feel obligated to have the implementation ignore the body in that case, which means adding extra `if`s in the body loop.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2802830415/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807971828","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105250#issuecomment-2807971828","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105250","id":2807971828,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nXj_0","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T01:46:28Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T01:46:28Z","body":"@jrouwe agreed, it does get a bit confusing when some of the search parameters are basically mutually exclusive.\r\n\r\nSo indeed that would suggest that adding `include` to the existing queries isn't a good idea. It would be better to have a new function call in the physics server that simply checks a ray cast against a single body RID as you suggested. I guess something like `bool body_intersect_ray(RID p_rid, Vector3 p_from, Vector3 p_to, RayResult &r_result);`?\r\n\r\nInteresting to see btw that we already define a type `RayResult` but return it as a Dictionary in the original `intersect_ray` implementation. I know this is for historic reasons but it would make sense to turn `RayResult` into a proper class (say `PhysicsRayResult3D`) and just return it as the result. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807971828/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2808607760","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105250#issuecomment-2808607760","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105250","id":2808607760,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nZ_QQ","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T07:09:08Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T07:09:08Z","body":"It might be worth considering passing e.g. an array of `RIDs` to test against rather than a single `RID`, because it allows both single and multiple tests, multiple tests could become prohibitively expensive with the single approach.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2808607760/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092228708","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105250#issuecomment-3092228708","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105250","id":3092228708,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64T6pk","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T09:59:35Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T09:59:35Z","body":"Closing this. I agree this should be handled differently. I don't plan to work on this (at least anytime soon).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092228708/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]